WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.766
During their journey across the Kalos region,

2
00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:08.833
our heroes visited the Muraille Coast,

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.966
before Ash's battle against Grant at the Cyllage City Gym.

4
00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:17.200
There was more training to come, but first, time for a delicious lunch.

5
00:00:17.266 --> 00:00:18.933
That was great, thanks!

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Time to train! Let's do some more work on Quick Attack and Double Team,

7
00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:25.433
so we can be ready for Grant's Rock Tomb!

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.166
- Froakie!
- Pikachu!

9
00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:30.900
Before that, why don't we have a little fun with this?

10
00:00:30.966 --> 00:00:35.366
Huh? That's one of the rods we got at Ambrette Aquarium!

11
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:37.500
Yup! We are at the beach.

12
00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:41.133
- Too much training will stress you out!
- She's right!

13
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.233
And maybe you'll catch a really, really cute Pokémon!

14
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.833
- Denne!
- Right, like with that Corsola!

15
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.933
You already have a Froakie, Ash, but if you catch another Water type,

16
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.866
you'll probably have a much easier time when you go up against Grant,

17
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:58.433
- who uses Rock types!
- Now you're talkin'! Great!

18
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.433
What do you say we get our rod?

19
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.266
Pikachu!

20
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.133
Can't wait to see what Pokémon I'll catch. I'm sure it'll be great!

21
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.033
Huh? I've got a bite!

22
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.400
- Pika!
- Froakie, kie!

23
00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:14.400
Man! This thing's pretty strong!

24
00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:17.900
- Ah!
- Oh goody, goody! What could it be?

25
00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:20.633
Corsola? A Clamperl or a Wailord?

26
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.533
Ah! I'm gonna catch it, no matter what!

27
00:01:27.466 --> 00:01:30.133
Ah!

28
00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:33.066
Huh?

29
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:39.133
- Too bad. It's just a bunch of kelp.
- Not true! He really caught something!

30
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.933
Huh?

31
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

32
00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:49.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

33
00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:53.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

34
00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:54.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

35
00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:58.433
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

36
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.633
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

37
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.500
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

38
00:02:04.566 --> 00:02:09.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

39
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

40
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

41
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.966
An Undersea Place to Call Home!

42
00:02:27.633 --> 00:02:31.033
That hurts! Man! I didn't know you were a Pokémon!

43
00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.666
- Hey! It's hurt!
- Huh?

44
00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:34.466
Wait. I've got a bandage.

45
00:02:35.766 --> 00:02:38.700
Mm. There. It'll be fine now!

46
00:02:41.266 --> 00:02:43.200
- Huh?

47
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.933
Skrelp. The Mock Kelp Pokémon.

48
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.333
Skrelp camouflages itself as rotten kelp,

49
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.600
while it stores up energy until it's able to evolve.

50
00:02:56.666 --> 00:02:58.833
Huh. I've never seen a Skrelp before!

51
00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.900
Skrelp-relp-relp!

52
00:03:01.966 --> 00:03:03.166
Why is it so mad?

53
00:03:03.233 --> 00:03:06.666
- Maybe it thinks we're its enemies.
- We're not!

54
00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:07.900
Pikachu, wait!

55
00:03:07.966 --> 00:03:09.700
Pika, pika!

56
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.866
Pika...

57
00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:15.533
Pikachu, no! Pikachu, are you OK?

58
00:03:16.533 --> 00:03:18.033
Skrelp!

59
00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.866
- Pikachu!
- Pikachu needs to get help right away!

60
00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.533
- The Pokémon Centre, now!
- Right!

61
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:30.500
Hi! Is something wrong?

62
00:03:30.566 --> 00:03:34.000
- My Pikachu was attacked and got hurt!
- Huh?

63
00:03:34.066 --> 00:03:37.000
It looks like it's been badly poisoned.

64
00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:40.133
Your Pikachu needs to be treated right now!

65
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.200
There should be an antidote in the first-aid kit.

66
00:03:46.533 --> 00:03:48.233
That should do it.

67
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.700
Pi? Pikachu!

68
00:03:50.766 --> 00:03:53.200
- Pikachu!
- Pika, pi!

69
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.933
You're all right! Thank you so much!

70
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.400
- I'm glad we were able to help.
- Hi! My name is Ash.

71
00:03:59.466 --> 00:04:02.333
- You already met my partner, Pikachu.
- Pikachu!

72
00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.433
- Hi, there! I'm Serena.
- My name's Bonnie.

73
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.166
This is Dedenne! That's my brother.

74
00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:11.366
Hi. My name's Clemont. -My name's Eddy.

75
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:15.133
- And this is my wife.
- I'm Lindsey. Nice to meet you!

76
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.566
Eddy and I are underwater archaeologists.

77
00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:20.166
Wow. Underwater archaeologists?

78
00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:25.466
- So... Are you exploring these waters?
- Yes. We'll be diving in that area today.

79
00:04:25.533 --> 00:04:27.533
- Huh?
- Pika?

80
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:34.766
Apparently there's a sunken ship called the Cussler in the vicinity.

81
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:36.333
-That sounds familiar.

82
00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.266
Didn't The Cussler crash into an iceberg long ago?

83
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:42.266
That's right. The Cussler was a luxury liner.

84
00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:58.866
Wait. I thought the Cussler sank way, way out into the ocean.

85
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:02.166
So why would it be over here, near the Muraille Coast?

86
00:05:02.233 --> 00:05:04.766
- Probably due to the currents.
- The currents?

87
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:08.433
Several ocean currents intersect here on the Muraille Coast.

88
00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.000
It creates a very complex current system.

89
00:05:11.066 --> 00:05:15.433
We believe that a current carried the Cussler all the way here.

90
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.500
- Whoa!
- Our research has one goal,

91
00:05:18.566 --> 00:05:22.266
to find the Cussler and identify the current that brought it here.

92
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:25.000
It's promising to be a very busy day today!

93
00:05:25.066 --> 00:05:28.000
Ocean exploration's so cool! It sounds fun!

94
00:05:28.066 --> 00:05:30.833
Is there any chance we could go along with you?

95
00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.833
- Pika?
- We'll help you with anything!

96
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.333
With my invention expertise, I'm certain I can help!

97
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.866
Huh? Hm.

98
00:05:38.933 --> 00:05:42.933
All right. You'd be a big help! We're actually a bit short-handed.

99
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.033
But you need to remember that it might be dangerous.

100
00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.600
So you'll have to listen to us. Is that a deal?

101
00:05:48.666 --> 00:05:49.833
- Deal!
- Pika!

102
00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.766
The Cussler, eh?

103
00:05:55.833 --> 00:06:00.100
The luxury liner that sank while carrying priceless treasures on board.

104
00:06:00.166 --> 00:06:02.366
If we can get our paws on that boat booty,

105
00:06:02.433 --> 00:06:04.933
we'll never have to balance our chequebook again!

106
00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.633
Just imagine it. We'll be awash in wealth!

107
00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.700
- Let's claim ours today!
- Yay!

108
00:06:12.766 --> 00:06:14.066
Wobbuffet!

109
00:06:19.433 --> 00:06:21.800
- Wow!
- Those complex currents

110
00:06:21.866 --> 00:06:23.866
are creating those giant whirlpools.

111
00:06:23.933 --> 00:06:26.366
Lindsey, it's almost time!

112
00:06:26.433 --> 00:06:28.766
All right. Everyone watch closely.

113
00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:29.866
Got you!

114
00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:37.600
- Ah! Look at that!
- The whirlpools!

115
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.566
- They're gone!
- Pika!

116
00:06:42.633 --> 00:06:47.066
The intersecting currents that create those whirlpools change regularly.

117
00:06:47.133 --> 00:06:49.033
As usual, they're right on schedule.

118
00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.300
You shouldn't be seeing them for a while now.

119
00:06:53.933 --> 00:06:57.000
All right, we're here! Let's get ready to dive!

120
00:07:02.266 --> 00:07:05.300
Wow! Are you gonna dive down in this submarine?

121
00:07:05.366 --> 00:07:08.533
- That's correct.
- Hey, can we all go with you?

122
00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.266
- Pikachu!
- That'd be awesome!

123
00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:14.400
- It'd be so much fun!
- Nenne-ne!

124
00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:16.866
Well, our submarine's not very large

125
00:07:16.933 --> 00:07:20.133
and there's only room for two other people to get inside.

126
00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.500
- Aw.
- No problem!

127
00:07:21.566 --> 00:07:24.733
I know how we can decide who gets to go, fair and square!

128
00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:31.233
The future is now, thanks to science! Clemontic Gear, on!

129
00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.133
I call it my No Hard Feelings, Fair and Square Lottery Device!

130
00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.833
Science is so amazing!

131
00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:37.966
Choose left or right,

132
00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:41.133
and my lottery device will take the guesswork out of who goes

133
00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.200
and decide it for you!

134
00:07:42.266 --> 00:07:44.500
Cool. So I'll choose left!

135
00:07:44.566 --> 00:07:45.700
I'll choose left, too!

136
00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.166
In that case, I'm going to pick right.

137
00:07:49.233 --> 00:07:51.200
OK, then I'll go with my brother!

138
00:07:52.766 --> 00:07:54.400
Lottery, go!

139
00:07:57.366 --> 00:07:58.866
Come on! Don't lose!

140
00:07:58.933 --> 00:08:00.900
- Go!
- Go! Go!

141
00:08:00.966 --> 00:08:02.433
- Come on!
- Go!

142
00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.766
- Yeah, we won!
- We won!

143
00:08:08.833 --> 00:08:11.200
Aww. And we lost.

144
00:08:11.266 --> 00:08:13.766
- I was counting on you!
- Nenne-ne!

145
00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:17.100
Well, science determined our fate fair and square,

146
00:08:17.166 --> 00:08:19.333
so no hard feelings.

147
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.866
- All right, off we go!
- Good luck.

148
00:08:24.933 --> 00:08:26.666
- You'll do great.
- Be careful!

149
00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:28.166
Mm.

150
00:08:38.966 --> 00:08:40.666
Ne-ne-nenne-nenne!

151
00:08:40.733 --> 00:08:42.733
- Have fun, guys!
- Take care of yourself!

152
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.733
- This is Lindsey. Eddy, do you copy?
- Affirmative.

153
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.766
You're loud and clear. And the video is clear, too.

154
00:08:52.833 --> 00:08:55.233
Great. Continuing to our destination.

155
00:08:56.233 --> 00:08:59.733
Wow! I can't believe all the Qwilfish!

156
00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.800
- There's a bunch of Octillery over here!
- Pika!

157
00:09:02.866 --> 00:09:06.033
Wow! Look at all the Water-type Pokémon!

158
00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.933
This is so totally amazing!

159
00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:12.233
- We're down really deep.
- Pika...

160
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.433
- We'll soon see the bottom of the ocean.
- Huh? Is that the same Skrelp?

161
00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.366
I think you're right. Look! The bandage!

162
00:09:20.433 --> 00:09:23.166
- I'm so glad it found its friends.
- Yeah.

163
00:09:25.933 --> 00:09:30.166
- Lindsey! What's going on?
- We're being swept along by the current!

164
00:09:30.233 --> 00:09:31.500
Uh-oh. Hold on tight!

165
00:09:34.533 --> 00:09:36.200
So it is there!

166
00:09:36.266 --> 00:09:38.966
Our theory about the current is proving to be correct!

167
00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:42.233
Lindsey, look out! It's so close!

168
00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.266
Don't worry! I'll handle things!

169
00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.566
Whoa. We're all right.

170
00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:53.233
- Pika.
- Good thing.

171
00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.833
Hey, look at that group of Skrelp!

172
00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.366
They're following the sunken ship!

173
00:09:57.433 --> 00:09:59.466
All right. Hang on!

174
00:09:59.533 --> 00:10:01.033
Right!

175
00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.566
- Oh, wow!
- I see it.

176
00:10:22.566 --> 00:10:23.933
The Milotic emblem!

177
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.433
- There's no doubt that's the Cussler!
- Right!

178
00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.500
Wow, what a discovery!

179
00:10:29.566 --> 00:10:33.166
We're witnessing history in the making, right before our eyes!

180
00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.233
Dragalge.

181
00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.866
Who's that Pokémon?

182
00:10:46.933 --> 00:10:52.066
Dragalge. The Mock Kelp Pokémon, and the evolved form of Skrelp.

183
00:10:52.133 --> 00:10:56.366
Dragalge look like drifting kelp when they are swimming with the current.

184
00:10:58.666 --> 00:11:00.666
Dragal.

185
00:11:00.733 --> 00:11:06.633
Huh? What are those two up to? Are they fusing the ships together?

186
00:11:08.233 --> 00:11:11.133
- It's a group of Luvdisc!

187
00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.433
Look! Remoraid and Chinchou are coming out, too!

188
00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.833
Pika!

189
00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.833
Dragalge. Dragalge. Dragalge.

190
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:25.200
Amazing, isn't it? The current carries sunken ships from faraway oceans.

191
00:11:25.266 --> 00:11:28.966
Once they get here, the Dragalge fuse them together using Acid,

192
00:11:29.033 --> 00:11:31.200
to create one gigantic structure.

193
00:11:31.266 --> 00:11:34.866
Then all the Pokémon are able to use that structure as their home!

194
00:11:34.933 --> 00:11:35.766
That's right.

195
00:11:35.833 --> 00:11:39.033
- They live together like one happy family!
- Nenne!

196
00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.100
They all get along so well, don't they?

197
00:11:43.166 --> 00:11:45.966
- They really like hanging out!
- Pikachu!

198
00:11:46.033 --> 00:11:49.600
Wow. It's like a Pokémon paradise. Wonderful!

199
00:11:49.666 --> 00:11:51.966
- Huh? What's that?
- Huh?

200
00:11:56.066 --> 00:11:58.933
- Light!
- What's it from?

201
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.900
Who's that Pokémon?

202
00:12:06.066 --> 00:12:07.833
It's Skrelp!

203
00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.500
Skrelp.

204
00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.333
What is it, Lindsey?

205
00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.566
I need to investigate a strange light coming from the Cussler.

206
00:12:19.633 --> 00:12:22.066
Right. Be careful.

207
00:12:31.633 --> 00:12:34.800
Ah! It's Team Rocket's submarine!

208
00:12:34.866 --> 00:12:38.666
- Team Rocket?!
- They're bad guys who steal Pokémon!

209
00:12:38.733 --> 00:12:40.800
So what is Team Rocket doing there?

210
00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.533
Dragalge.

211
00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.633
They just went inside the old ship!

212
00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.066
I think we should follow them!

213
00:12:49.133 --> 00:12:50.500
Right!

214
00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:01.100
- Gettin' in was easy-peasy.
- Wo-wobbuffet!

215
00:13:01.166 --> 00:13:05.166
- Now to locate the treasure.
- It's in a safe just up ahead.

216
00:13:05.233 --> 00:13:08.800
- All valuables were stored there.
- Not for long!

217
00:13:08.866 --> 00:13:11.233
Wobba-wobba-wobba!

218
00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:14.600
Skrelp. Skrelp.

219
00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:22.333
They're not here. Which way did they go?

220
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.866
- Pika, pi?
- Huh?

221
00:13:23.933 --> 00:13:25.200
Is something wrong?

222
00:13:25.266 --> 00:13:27.266
Skrelp and Dragalge!

223
00:13:29.533 --> 00:13:33.800
- Stop it! We're on your side. Promise!
- Pika, pika!

224
00:13:33.866 --> 00:13:34.866
Skrelp.

225
00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.600
Hey, thanks, Skrelp.

226
00:13:39.666 --> 00:13:42.766
Skrelp.

227
00:13:42.833 --> 00:13:44.766
They're showing us which way to go!

228
00:13:44.833 --> 00:13:46.933
Pick, pick here, pick, pick there.

229
00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.666
- I'm done first!
- Well, so are we!

230
00:13:48.733 --> 00:13:51.166
Wow. On the other side of this door...

231
00:13:51.233 --> 00:13:53.400
A treasure trove of treasure awaits!

232
00:13:53.466 --> 00:13:55.000
Wo-wobba!

233
00:13:55.066 --> 00:13:58.066
- Hey!
- What was that?

234
00:13:58.133 --> 00:14:00.766
Skrelp, Skrelp, Skrelp, Skrelp. Skrelp.

235
00:14:00.833 --> 00:14:02.366
Oh. It's a Skrelp.

236
00:14:02.433 --> 00:14:06.500
It's tellin' us to scram out of its digs, or we're gonna pay!

237
00:14:06.566 --> 00:14:10.033
Ha! You're confused. We're going to get paid!

238
00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.366
Wobbuffet!

239
00:14:11.433 --> 00:14:12.500
- Stop right there!
- Huh?

240
00:14:12.566 --> 00:14:15.400
We caught you guys red-handed!

241
00:14:15.466 --> 00:14:17.900
What is the meaning of you breaking into this ship?

242
00:14:17.966 --> 00:14:20.666
Prepare for trouble, the meaning is clear!

243
00:14:20.733 --> 00:14:22.900
But it isn't something you'll want to hear

244
00:14:22.966 --> 00:14:25.400
To protect the world from devastation!

245
00:14:25.466 --> 00:14:28.033
To unite all people within our nation!

246
00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.400
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

247
00:14:31.466 --> 00:14:33.900
To extend our reach to the stars above!

248
00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.466
- Jessie!
- And James.

249
00:14:36.533 --> 00:14:40.000
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

250
00:14:40.066 --> 00:14:43.066
Surrender now or prepare for one Wailord-sized fight!

251
00:14:43.133 --> 00:14:46.600
- Meowth, that's right!
- Wobbuffet!

252
00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.900
If you had half a brain between you,

253
00:14:49.966 --> 00:14:52.000
you'd know we're here for sunken treasure!

254
00:14:52.066 --> 00:14:53.800
We'll balance our chequebook

255
00:14:53.866 --> 00:14:56.833
on the back of the beautiful bounty on this boat!

256
00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:59.033
- Wobba!
- Sunken treasure?

257
00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.200
How do you think you'll get away with that?

258
00:15:01.266 --> 00:15:03.933
You're so dense. Watch and learn!

259
00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.933
The latest in bank robberosity!

260
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.133
In mere moments, this safe is going to blast off!

261
00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.600
And that blast-off will be a good thing!

262
00:15:12.666 --> 00:15:16.100
Ah!

263
00:15:16.166 --> 00:15:19.833
Where are you going?

264
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:23.333
- Come back!
- No! It's dangerous!

265
00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.666
Froakie, come out and follow Skrelp!

266
00:15:28.966 --> 00:15:31.666
Froakie! Froak, froak, froak!

267
00:15:31.733 --> 00:15:34.500
- Pika, pika!
- Hope they'll be all right.

268
00:15:34.566 --> 00:15:35.900
- We've got to leave!
- Huh?

269
00:15:35.966 --> 00:15:39.900
If that explosion opens up a hole, water will flood the whole area!

270
00:15:39.966 --> 00:15:41.933
- Hurry!
- Pika!

271
00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:59.666
- One treasure, coming up!
- Yes. Let's reel her in!

272
00:16:02.166 --> 00:16:04.333
- Huh? Not you!
- Not you who?

273
00:16:08.233 --> 00:16:09.633
Froakie !

274
00:16:10.833 --> 00:16:13.566
Yet another eyesore! You're blocking my view!

275
00:16:13.633 --> 00:16:16.066
Off, off, off, off, off, off, off!

276
00:16:19.633 --> 00:16:22.300
The Cussler is filling with water!

277
00:16:22.366 --> 00:16:25.400
The entire structure is starting to become unbalanced.

278
00:16:25.466 --> 00:16:27.600
- I'm afraid it's going to collapse.
- No!

279
00:16:27.666 --> 00:16:30.533
We've gotta do something to keep that from happening!

280
00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:34.166
- Pikachu!
- Everyone, we need your help!

281
00:16:35.233 --> 00:16:39.566
Dragalge!

282
00:16:39.633 --> 00:16:41.333
- Dragal.
- Luvdisc!

283
00:16:43.433 --> 00:16:46.833
Froakie-e-e-e!

284
00:16:49.066 --> 00:16:50.800
The safe is safe!

285
00:16:50.866 --> 00:16:53.666
- Surface, stat!
- Aye, aye!

286
00:16:54.866 --> 00:16:56.900
- Froak!

287
00:17:12.566 --> 00:17:15.233
- Awesome!
- Yeah! Hope they keep it up!

288
00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.300
Just a little more.

289
00:17:19.366 --> 00:17:23.633
Lindsey, use that plate to seal the hole!

290
00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.533
Got it!

291
00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.766
Now, Dragalge! Use Acid!

292
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.766
Great! That should prevent any more water from flooding the ship!

293
00:17:38.833 --> 00:17:40.966
The structure should stop collapsing, too!

294
00:17:41.033 --> 00:17:43.633
- All right!
- Pika!

295
00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.166
Great job! That was a tough one.

296
00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:49.133
- Eddy!
- But you're all safe and sound.

297
00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.000
And that's what matters to me the most.

298
00:17:51.066 --> 00:17:54.833
It's time. The whirlpools are going to appear again soon!

299
00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.033
Right!

300
00:18:01.733 --> 00:18:05.400
- Success! Have treasure, will travel!
- Wobbuffet!

301
00:18:05.466 --> 00:18:09.366
Yeah. Now we'll have balanced books and be off those tenterhooks!

302
00:18:09.433 --> 00:18:10.633
Froak!

303
00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:14.633
Hm. Huh? Ugh, is something swirling out there?

304
00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.933
- Huh?
- Huh?

305
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.633
- Over there, too!
- Uh-oh!

306
00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.933
- There's another one!
- Argh!

307
00:18:23.733 --> 00:18:26.133
We're spinning faster and faster!

308
00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.166
I'm gettin' dizzier and dizzier!

309
00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.400
We dropped the safe!

310
00:18:32.466 --> 00:18:36.000
- Butterfingers!
- The scent of regret lingers!

311
00:18:36.066 --> 00:18:37.866
We're blasting off again!

312
00:18:37.933 --> 00:18:39.966
Wobbuffet!

313
00:18:45.366 --> 00:18:47.500
Where's Skrelp and Froakie?

314
00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:52.666
- Froakie, froak!
- Skrelp, Skrelp!

315
00:18:52.733 --> 00:18:53.566
Oh, no!

316
00:18:53.633 --> 00:18:56.233
Even Water types can't withstand a whirlpool!

317
00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.300
Now what?

318
00:18:57.366 --> 00:19:00.800
- Froakie, you've gotta jump!
- Pika!

319
00:19:00.866 --> 00:19:03.766
Froa! Kie, kie, froa!

320
00:19:03.833 --> 00:19:05.266
Froa!

321
00:19:06.233 --> 00:19:09.333
Froa, Froakie!

322
00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:13.000
Froa, froa, froa!

323
00:19:13.066 --> 00:19:14.933
Now, Froakie, big jump!

324
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.600
Froakieeeee!

325
00:19:19.666 --> 00:19:23.466
Ha!

326
00:19:23.533 --> 00:19:24.866
- Froakie!
- Froakie!

327
00:19:24.933 --> 00:19:26.000
Great!

328
00:19:26.066 --> 00:19:27.366
- They did it!
- Denne!

329
00:19:27.433 --> 00:19:28.400
Hm.

330
00:19:28.466 --> 00:19:29.866
- Thank goodness!
- Perfect!

331
00:19:29.933 --> 00:19:32.366
Froakie, you were awesome!

332
00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:34.333
Skrelp, you were awesome, too!

333
00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.866
- Kie, froa!
- Skrelp, Skrelp, Skrelp!

334
00:19:41.933 --> 00:19:45.600
- Bye, Skrelp! Bye, Dragalge!
- Take care of your home

335
00:19:45.666 --> 00:19:49.233
- and all of those friends of yours!
- Pikachu!

336
00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.366
Take good care, Skrelp!

337
00:19:55.433 --> 00:19:57.966
- Hope we see you again!
- Skrelp!

338
00:19:59.033 --> 00:20:02.833
Happily, we were able to figure out which current brought the Cussler

339
00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.400
and successfully pinpoint its location, too.

340
00:20:05.466 --> 00:20:09.266
What surprised me the most was seeing all those Pokémon living together.

341
00:20:09.333 --> 00:20:10.700
That was some discovery!

342
00:20:10.766 --> 00:20:13.500
And Skrelp's OK, thanks to your jump!

343
00:20:13.566 --> 00:20:15.933
- You're such a cool Pokémon!
- Froa, froa.

344
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.466
The height of that jump was just incredible!

345
00:20:18.533 --> 00:20:20.733
Wow. You should be really proud of yourself!

346
00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:21.933
That was some jump.

347
00:20:25.466 --> 00:20:26.666
Pikachu.

348
00:20:26.733 --> 00:20:30.900
Hey, maybe we could use that in our Gym Battle against Grant.

349
00:20:30.966 --> 00:20:32.633
- Pika!
- That's it! Of course we can!

350
00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:34.633
Froakie!

351
00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:38.900
And so, Froakie's brilliance rescued Skrelp from the whirlpool,

352
00:20:38.966 --> 00:20:42.766
and also gave Ash an idea for his battle at the Cyllage City Gym,

353
00:20:42.833 --> 00:20:46.433
the next stop on our heroes' journey!
